  "notes": "The Suave House line, and the research calls it the most harmonically rich lane in Memphis — which makes it the one entry on this axis that overrides the parent's harmony wholesale rather than tightening it. Minor-7 and dominant-9 voicings with ii–v–i and i–iv–V motion borrowed from Memphis soul means `extensions` inverts the parent's 92% triad reading, `maxChords` rises to 4 and `topVoiceStepwise` comes back on. The single feature the research says separates them from the Hypnotize board is the bass: walking electric/synth lines that outline the changes rather than sitting on the root, so `bassline.rhythm` is `independent_riff` with `followRootsProb` 0.5 and a 19-semitone register — the only Memphis entry in this batch that genuinely moves. Drums go the other way: \"raw music untainted with flashy technological flourishes\" and \"restrained fills\" put the perc lanes at their quietest and the kick at two or three thuds a bar. The keyboard answering the vocal is a real described part, so the countermelody carries weight here instead of sitting at the floor. ⚠ `medium` rather than high: the research rates it high-medium and marks the tempo band **[LOW-CONF]** — `session.bpm` (68–80 half-time = 136–160 straight) is inferred from the lane, not documented for them. Instrumentation, drum character and the harmonic register are sourced. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 47 to 43 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 44 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 4.",
